# Docker build context filter.
#
# Without this file the context is the whole repository — and in this workspace
# that is roughly 27 GB, dominated by .turbo (13 GB), .worktrees (11 GB) and
# node_modules (1.8 GB). BuildKit walks and hashes every byte of the context on
# every build, so leaving those in makes builds slow regardless of layer caching.
#
# Keep this list in sync with the COPY instructions in infra/docker/*.Dockerfile.
# Anything a Dockerfile COPYs must NOT be excluded here. Currently those are:
#   root:      package.json, pnpm-lock.yaml, pnpm-workspace.yaml, .npmrc
#   packages/: config/{package.json,tsconfig}, shared, validators, ui,
#              mobile-core/{package.json,tsconfig.json,src,assets}
#   apps/api:  package.json, tsconfig.json, src, scripts, prisma,
#              prisma.config.ts
#   apps/admin: package.json, tsconfig.json, next.config.mjs,
#              postcss.config.mjs, src
#   apps/mobile|driver: package.json, tsconfig.json, metro.config.js, app.json,
#              app, src, assets, (mobile only) public
#   infra/:    docker/ (nginx-expo.conf), seed/ (demo-manifest.json)

# ── Dependency trees (reinstalled inside the image) ──
node_modules
**/node_modules

# ── Build caches and worktrees ──
.turbo
**/.turbo
.worktrees
.git
.github

# ── Build output (each Dockerfile regenerates what it needs) ──
**/dist
**/.next
**/.expo
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Local runtime data ──
apps/api/uploads
uploads
storage
tmp
temp

# ── Secrets: injected through compose env_file, never COPYed into an image ──
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# ── Documentation and tooling not referenced by any Dockerfile ──
docs
design-preview
.agent
.agents
.superpowers
*.md
**/*.md

# ── Editor / OS noise ──
**/*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea
.vscode
